{
  "_comment": [
      "A MINIMAL MILAN v1.2 ENTITY MODEL: the semantic lint's positive case.",
      "",
      "gen_desc_image.py packs it with its semantic lint on (model_lint.py,",
      "docs/architecture/07 \u00a73.1 rules L1 to L11), and the descriptor-packer",
      "gate (tb/desc_store/test_gen_desc_image.py) derives every negative case",
      "from it by one named mutation. Its entity_model_id and digest are",
      "recorded in model_ids.json; change a descriptor field outside the",
      "IEEE 1722.1-2021 \u00a76.2.2.8 exclusions and the id has to change with it.",
      "",
      "One configuration: an AAF Talker with one Stream Output, and a Listener",
      "with one AAF Stream Input and the CRF Media Clock Input an AAF Talker",
      "needs (Milan v1.2 \u00a77.2.2). Base formats only (Milan v1.2 \u00a76.2): the",
      "input advertises 48 kHz up to 8 channels with the ut bit, the output",
      "48 kHz stereo. One AUDIO_UNIT at 48 kHz, one Stream Port per direction",
      "with two mono AUDIO_CLUSTERs each; the output port maps its stream",
      "statically, the input port has no AUDIO_MAP (Milan v1.2 \u00a75.3.3.7). An",
      "INTERNAL and a CRF INPUT_STREAM CLOCK_SOURCE, one CLOCK_DOMAIN listing",
      "both, and the primary IDENTIFY CONTROL at index 0.",
      "",
      "Stream descriptors use the IEEE 1722.1-2021 Table 7-8 layout",
      "(formats_offset 138, no redundancy tail), as a shipping model does.",
      "Identity values are locally administered placeholders: this repository",
      "ships no vendor's entity model. NOT example_milan_8.json, which is a",
      "layout vector packed with the lint off."
  ],
